# Copy to .env.local in this directory (apps/console/.env.local, gitignored
# via the repo's .env* rule — never commit the real file) and restart the
# dev server. See README.md's Setup section for context.

# Base Sepolia (chain 84532) RPC endpoint(s) the browser uses for every read
# and write the maker console makes. Optional -- falls back to Base
# Sepolia's shared public RPC if unset, but that endpoint rate-/size-limits
# requests ("Request exceeds defined limit") once more than a couple of
# strategy cards are polling at once.
#
# Comma-separated list = a fallback chain: wagmi tries each in order and
# moves to the next on error, so no single public endpoint's limit or
# uptime is the whole story. A paid provider (Alchemy/Infura/etc.) works
# too, alone or mixed in with public ones. Must be prefixed with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ since wagmi's config runs in the browser, not just at build
# time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://base-sepolia.gateway.tenderly.co,https://base-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com,https://base-sepolia.rpc.sentio.xyz,https://base-testnet.api.pocket.network,https://base-sepolia-public.nodies.app

# Same idea for Ethereum Sepolia (chain 11155111) and Arbitrum Sepolia
# (chain 421614), reachable from the navbar's network switcher. Optional --
# lib/chain.ts already ships a multi-endpoint fallback list for each
# (not wagmi/viem's own defaults, which are shared-by-every-anonymous-dapp
# endpoints that rate-limit hard), so these only need setting to override
# with your own provider.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ETH_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com,https://rpc.sepolia.ethpandaops.io,https://eth-sepolia-testnet.api.pocket.network
NEXT_PUBLIC_ARBITRUM_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://arbitrum-sepolia.gateway.tenderly.co,https://sepolia-rollup.arbitrum.io/rpc,https://arbitrum-sepolia.drpc.org
